  "details": "It would be great if there was an official benchmarking world (with accompanying avatar that would be recommended to wear).\n\nAt the moment benchmarking VRC is a bit difficult; the nature of worlds and avatars being as dynamic as they are inherently means results are inconsistent.\n\nLikewise, just going into empty worlds only really allows you to see the impacts your GPU has on render time.\n\nHaving a world that loads CPU and GPU (and simulates X amount of players) would be great; it 'd allow users to be able to share and compare their results to help pinpoint the best hardware configurations for VRCHat.\n\nHeck, there could even be leaderboards potentially.\n\nIt'd be a fun little competition while also allowing devs and players alike to hone in on the hardware and software quirks of VRChat and potentially discover new combinations of hardware that benefit the playerbase.\n\nOn the dev side, often optimizations in software can be found by noting what types of hardware have the biggest impacts as well.\n\nStated otherwise; it's all well and good to claim that the 5800X3D/7800X3D is the single best CPU for VRChat; it's another thing to have the data to back it up.",
